  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "radiotap: Improve indication of 6 GHz band channels",
  "description": "Update the channel information string for the 6 GHz band.\nUse \"6 GHz\"; should the current \"BG\" and \"A\" perhaps be replaced\nwith \"2.4 GHz\" and \"5 GHz\" as the current labels are somewhat\nanachronistic now?\n    \nAdd a comment about 802.11ax certified devices and control frames,\nwhich are transmitted in legacy mode using the basic rate of\n6 Mb/s (MCS 0); with no HE or EHT field in the radiotap header,\nthese are shown as PHY_11A, which may be confusing to users.)\n\nFix #17393",
  "state": "merged",
