        {
          "id": 1625927753,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "`Keep PHDR_802_11_PHY_11G` - currently it reports `PHDR_802_11_PHY_11A` because the 5 GHz bit is set (and the 2.4 GHz bit is not.)\n\nSo you would prefer if basic rate frames in legacy mode in the 6 GHz band indicate `PHDR_802_11_PHY_11A` (or changed to `PHDR_802_11_PHY_11G`)? I do understand the argument, it's a difference between 802.11ax the standard and the PHY mode.\n\nThat seems fine, I think it would just make sense to close #17393 anyway then after changing how the channels are described.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
